WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.003 --> 00:00:03.177
- People, the world's teeming with them.

00:00:03.177 --> 00:00:05.817
I'm a person, you're probably a person

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:08.397
and everyone you know,
they're people, too.

00:00:08.397 --> 00:00:09.977
And we're all different.

00:00:09.977 --> 00:00:13.336
A bus driver isn't the same
as a candlestick maker.

00:00:13.336 --> 00:00:15.165
Your local mail carrier isn't the same

00:00:15.165 --> 00:00:17.071
as Supreme Court Justice
Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:00:17.071 --> 00:00:18.695
And that's great because
the world would be

00:00:18.695 --> 00:00:20.735
kind of stupid if we were all the same.

00:00:20.735 --> 00:00:22.474
So let's see what we can learn

00:00:22.474 --> 00:00:24.235
by talking to a real person.

00:00:24.235 --> 00:00:26.922
Let's see what we can learn by talking

00:00:26.922 --> 00:00:28.172
to Mr. Leather.

00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:32.558
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:32.558 --> 00:00:33.978
We've all seen beauty pageants.

00:00:33.978 --> 00:00:35.778
They're kind of weird,
a little out of touch,

00:00:35.778 --> 00:00:36.998
maybe a little polite.

00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:38.038
I mean, look at this.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.998
What are these, what are these hoops?

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:40.831
What?

00:00:40.831 --> 00:00:42.081
This is boring.

00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:47.232
- [Voiceover] Oh okay, see.

00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:49.332
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about.

00:00:49.332 --> 00:00:53.507
What you're seeing here is
Mr. Los Angeles Leather 2016.

00:00:53.507 --> 00:00:56.090
Whoever overcomes the stiff competition

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.270
will go on to compete
against fellow Mr. Leathers

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.051
from around the world with the hopes of

00:01:00.051 --> 00:01:03.150
becoming International Mr. Leather 2016.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.210
This hallowed contest
has been held annually

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.591
since 1979, but before we dig too deep.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:11.591
Can you sum up Mr. Leather in a few words?

00:01:11.591 --> 00:01:14.891
- Miss Universe of the gay, leather world.

00:01:14.891 --> 00:01:16.031
- Alright, yeah.

00:01:16.031 --> 00:01:17.290
That's a few words.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.930
That man on the right, the one

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.550
that looks like an ad for sex cologne,

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.830
is International Mr.
Leather 2015, Patrick Smith.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.830
- The Leather Community is largely

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.047
a subset of the LGBT community.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:32.206
It's for guys who dress
up in their leather

00:01:32.206 --> 00:01:34.566
and it makes them feel confident and sexy.

00:01:34.566 --> 00:01:36.844
Leather culture's been
around since, they say

00:01:36.844 --> 00:01:39.965
it probably dates back
to post-World War Two,

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:42.565
when a lot of the guys
came back from overseas

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:44.745
and they remained in the coastal cities

00:01:44.745 --> 00:01:48.325
and wore their hypermasculine,
leather uniforms.

00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:49.885
Nowadays, though, you see leather

00:01:49.885 --> 00:01:51.206
including all sorts of people.

00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:52.745
Masculine, feminine, it doesn't matter.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.385
- [Shane] And the contestants
vying for the title

00:01:54.385 --> 00:01:56.665
of Mr. Leather are all
different sorts of people.

00:01:56.665 --> 00:01:59.330
Young and old, Djs, business owners,

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.324
community activists, fathers.

00:02:01.324 --> 00:02:03.044
But they've all got one thing in common,

00:02:03.044 --> 00:02:05.282
they're damn proud of who they are.

00:02:05.282 --> 00:02:09.199
♫ Gave proof through the night

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:14.664
♫ That our flag was still there ♫

00:02:15.897 --> 00:02:17.657
- [Shane] What's involved
with the contest?

00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:19.357
- You go out, you give a speech

00:02:19.357 --> 00:02:20.937
wearing your full leather uniform.

00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:22.738
- I look out into the audience tonight

00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:23.827
and I know there are a lot

00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:25.596
of hot, kinky (beep) out there.

00:02:25.596 --> 00:02:28.476
- I would be very proud and honored

00:02:28.476 --> 00:02:32.092
to represent us as L.A. Mr. Leather.

00:02:32.092 --> 00:02:33.732
- Do you wear like one sort of outfit

00:02:33.732 --> 00:02:35.192
for the whole thing or is it like a--

00:02:35.192 --> 00:02:37.392
- No, it's all sorts of different looks.

00:02:37.392 --> 00:02:38.657
- It's like Whoopi Goldberg at the Oscars.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:39.490
- Exactly.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.697
(sexy Jazz music)

00:02:41.697 --> 00:02:43.184
You slowly start shedding the clothing

00:02:43.184 --> 00:02:44.017
throughout the night.

00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:44.850
- [Shane] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.291
- So it goes into the harnesses,
getting a little slutty.

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.610
- That's how it happens, yeah.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:51.360
See, just like Whoopi
Goldberg at the Oscars.

00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:55.949
As the outgoing International Mr. Leather,

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:58.409
Patrick sits behind the
judges' table this year,

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:00.149
prepared to give up the title,

00:03:00.149 --> 00:03:01.389
but it's been a busy year for him.

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:02.749
The title is more than just looking good

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.169
in a piece of cow hide, there's a

00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:05.769
philanthropist side as well.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.609
- I spent four years up in Canada

00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:09.309
working in politics and a lot of people

00:03:09.309 --> 00:03:13.349
have done very political
things and activist things

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:14.369
with leather titles.

00:03:14.369 --> 00:03:15.989
So that was sort of what drew me into

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:17.589
that aspect of it.

00:03:17.589 --> 00:03:19.489
So I've been traveling all over the world

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:22.434
to places where it's pretty
scary to be gay still.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.887
So I went to Uganda, I
went to Egypt and Morocco

00:03:24.887 --> 00:03:26.508
and the Ukraine and places where people

00:03:26.508 --> 00:03:30.528
are jailed or murdered
just for being openly gay.

00:03:30.528 --> 00:03:32.208
So my goal was to go out to these places,

00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:33.768
learn what the situation is over there

00:03:33.768 --> 00:03:35.987
and come back and do
fundraising and raise awareness

00:03:35.987 --> 00:03:37.568
for their situations.

00:03:37.568 --> 00:03:39.028
- [Shane] And in the
same way that they fight

00:03:39.028 --> 00:03:41.228
for the rights of the
LGBT community at large,

00:03:41.228 --> 00:03:43.268
these guys also fight for each other.

00:03:43.268 --> 00:03:47.028
- Some point in my life, I
stopped including myself.

00:03:47.028 --> 00:03:49.328
But it was my leather family, they were

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.727
the ones that came and
said, "David, come back.

00:03:51.727 --> 00:03:54.728
We want you just the way you are."

00:03:54.728 --> 00:03:56.747
- [Shane] When it comes
down to it, the world

00:03:56.747 --> 00:03:58.528
isn't as accepting as we'd like to be,

00:03:58.528 --> 00:04:00.807
but in spite of that, there's
a lot of love out there.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:03.948
- The friendship, the
support, the diversity,

00:04:03.948 --> 00:04:06.808
the mentorship, it is what defines us

00:04:06.808 --> 00:04:08.547
and it's what makes us strong.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.328
We open doors for each other.

00:04:10.328 --> 00:04:12.787
That is why representing
this title for you

00:04:12.787 --> 00:04:15.787
has been among the
greatest honors of my life.

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:17.267
- [Shane] How's it feel after this year?

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.508
- You know, it's bittersweet.

00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:21.528
On one hand, it'll be nice
to have lazy Saturdays

00:04:21.528 --> 00:04:22.748
on the couch back.

00:04:22.748 --> 00:04:24.407
On the other hand, it's
a really cool feeling

00:04:24.407 --> 00:04:27.408
walking into a venue and
everybody knowing who you are

00:04:27.408 --> 00:04:29.247
and what your name is
and everything like that.

00:04:29.247 --> 00:04:30.747
- [Shane] You're not
gonna be forgotten though.

00:04:30.747 --> 00:04:33.928
- No, I'll fade slowly into
obscurity is more like it.

00:04:33.928 --> 00:04:35.308
- You'll just disappear.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.927
- I love you, Los Angeles.

00:04:36.927 --> 00:04:38.648
It has been a privilege and a honor.

00:04:38.648 --> 00:04:39.567
Thank you.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:43.028
(audience applauds)

00:04:43.028 --> 00:04:44.407
- [Shane] I learned a
lot from Mr. Leather,

00:04:44.407 --> 00:04:46.208
but above all else, you
should be passionate

00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:48.168
about the things that make you unique.

00:04:48.168 --> 00:04:50.307
Wear your identity fiercely,
even if that involves

00:04:50.307 --> 00:04:53.168
throwing on some nice, ass-less chaps

00:04:53.168 --> 00:04:56.188
and letting those little
butt cheeks hang out.

00:04:56.188 --> 00:04:59.788
Yeah, that's a good
thing to learn, I guess.

00:04:59.788 --> 00:05:02.371
(gentle music)

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:07.328
- [Voiceover] Your Mr. L.A. Leather 2016,

00:05:07.328 --> 00:05:08.616
Jeffrey Erdman.

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:10.745
